NeuroCore™ / Invariance-055 Pipeline
This repository contains the computational pipeline for the identification and validation of the 0.55 Invariant, an equilibrium signature developed within the ASHI Core framework.

🧠 Concept
The 0.55 Invariant is not a simple static value, but a criticality threshold identified through the application of Percolation Theory across heterogeneous datasets.
The framework suggests that complex systems—whether artificial neural network weights or bio-physiological signals such as EEG or fNIRS—tend to converge toward a common equilibrium point when subjected to logarithmic flow normalization.

🚀 Pipeline Features
Cross-Domain Validation
Comparative analysis across domains, including neural network weight distributions (Neural_Network_Weights) and biological spike trains (Neuro_Spike_Train).
Asymptotic Convergence
The system reaches 96.1% stability, supporting reproducibility of the extracted signature across varying data volumes.
Signal-Agnostic Design
The pipeline can extract the stability constant from inputs with different sampling frequencies while maintaining minimal jitter (0.00%).

